---
/**
 * Privacy policy. Confirming an order does store it (see /api/order-submissions),
 * but with no personal information attached — so this page has to say what is
 * kept without overclaiming in either direction. If the submission payload ever
 * grows a name, phone or IP, this page has to change with it.
 */
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { db } from '@/db/client';
const settings = await db.query.storeSettings.findFirst();
const storeName = settings?.name ?? 'We';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="What this website does and does not collect.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500">Last updated 1 August 2026</p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      This website does not collect your personal information. There is no account to make and no
      form that sends us your details — not your name, not your phone number, not your address.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">The order you build here</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      While you are adding dishes, that list is saved in your own browser, on your own device, so
      it survives a refresh or an interrupting phone call. Clearing your browser data — or tapping
      <span class="font-medium">Start over</span> — erases it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-bold">When you confirm an order</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      Tapping <span class="font-medium">Confirm order</span> saves the dishes, the quantities and
      the total to {storeName}, and gives you back an order number to quote on the phone. Saved
      alongside it: the time of day, and which browser and screen size you used. That is the whole
      record — no name, no phone number, and not your IP address. {storeName} uses it to see which
      dishes people actually want and when, so the kitchen can prepare for it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-bold">When you call us</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      Ordering happens on the phone. We take your name and what you want so we can cook it and hand
      it to the right person at the counter — the same as if you walked in. We do not add you to a
      mailing list, and we do not sell or share anything with anyone.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-bold">Analytics and cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      No tracking cookies, no advertising pixels, no third-party analytics.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-bold">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
      Call <a href={`tel:${settings?.phone}`} class="font-semibold underline underline-offset-4"
        >{settings?.phone}</a
      > or come by {settings?.address}.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
